# EF5560 术语表（中英对照 · 统一译名）

> **用途**：统一全课译名，避免同一个英文在不同笔记里出现两种中文。
> **考试用英文作答**，因此「考试可用的英文定义」列优先抄讲义原句；讲义没有的，标注来源。
> 跨课程通用的条目已另行登记在 [[EF5560_Fintech_and_AI_in_Finance/_meta/待并入术语总表|待并入术语总表]]，由主 agent 合并进 `_meta/术语总表.md`。

**来源标记**：`讲` = 讲义原文｜`🎙️` = 课堂转录｜`💡` = 笔记补充｜`大纲` = syllabus / 官方目录

---

## 1. AI 辅助编码

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Vibe Coding**（保留英文，中文可写「AI 辅助编码」） | Vibe Coding / AI-assisted coding | Describe the task in plain language, let an AI assistant write and run a small Python job, inspect the result, and revise until the output passes explicit checks. | M01 §2.2 | 讲 p.7 |
| 六步循环 | Six-step procedure | Define → give a precise instruction → run without editing first → inspect rows and plots → challenge timing and logic → fix, save, and document. | M01 §2.2.2 | 讲 p.9 |
| 六项规格 | Six specifications | Language and packages; data; price convention; forecast clock; predictors; outputs and checks. | M01 §2.2.3 | 讲 p.10 |
| 桌面编码工具 | Desktop coding tool | An AI tool that can read local files and execute code, as opposed to a chatbot that can only print code. | M01 §2.2.4 | 🎙️`43:06` |
| 权限分级 | Permission levels | The scope of local file and command access granted to an AI agent; start with the most restrictive. | M01 §2.2.4 | 🎙️`44:00` |
| 代码留痕 / 代码备份 | Code backup | Saving the generated code for every result, so that a mistake can be traced later. | M01 §2.2.4 | 🎙️`01:06:31` |
| 挑战式检验 | Challenge the output | Using your own knowledge of the data to contradict the AI's result (e.g. 200 prices must give 199 returns). | M01 §2.4.3 | 🎙️`47:59` |
| 幻觉 | Hallucination | AI-generated numbers that look plausible but are fabricated. | M01 §2.4.5 | 🎙️`01:22:11` |

## 2. 收益、价格与风险

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **简单收益** | Simple return | `r_t = P_t / P_{t−1} − 1` | M01 §2.3.1 | 讲 p.19 |
| **复合年增长率** | CAGR / Compound annual growth rate | The geometric annual growth implied by starting and ending capital over the actual number of price intervals; 240 prices contain 239 intervals. | M01 §2.3.4 | 恒生价格指数样本 1.511468%/年，不含股息 |
| **对数收益** | Log return | `r_t = ln(P_t / P_{t−1})` | M01 §2.3.1 | 讲 p.20 图注 |
| 收盘价 | Closing price | The last traded price of the period. | M01 §2.3.2 | 讲 p.22 |
| **复权收盘价** | Adjusted close | A price series adjusted for splits and dividends to place prices on a comparable economic basis. | M01 §2.3.2 | 讲 p.22 |
| 拆股 | Stock split | A split changes the quoted price without creating an investor loss. | M01 §2.3.2 | 讲 p.22 |
| 现金股利 | Cash dividend | Cash received is one component of total return; it does not guarantee a positive total return if the price loss is larger. | M01 §2.3.2 | 讲 p.22 |
| 价格指数 | Price index | An index that excludes dividends. | M01 §2.3.3 | 讲 p.18 |
| 全收益（指数） | Total return | A return measure that includes dividends. | M01 §2.3.3 | 讲 p.11 图注 |
| **波动率（年化）** | Annualized volatility | Under the stated square-root-of-time approximation, period return standard deviation times the square root of periods per year; serial dependence requires covariance-aware treatment and a disclosed sample denominator. | M01 §2.3.4 | 讲 p.44 |
| **回撤 / 最大回撤** | Drawdown / Maximum drawdown | The loss relative to the running historical peak; zero means the current value is at that peak, not that every recent subperiod avoided losses. | M01 §2.9.2 | 讲 p.51 |
| **基准** | Benchmark | The reference return a strategy must beat before its performance means anything. | M01 §2.3.3 | 🎙️`30:50` |
| 无风险资产 | Risk-free asset | A government bond repaid in its own currency. | M01 §2.3.3 | 🎙️`50:44` |
| 国债收益率 | Treasury yield | The yield on government debt; the 10-year is the standard reference. | M01 §2.3.3 | 🎙️`31:01` |
| **期限利差** | Term spread | Long-term yield minus the short-term policy rate; inversion is one recession-risk signal, not a guarantee that a recession must occur. | M01 §2.9.2 | 讲 p.32 ＋ 🎙️`01:48:20` |
| 联邦基金利率 | Federal funds rate (DFF) | The interbank overnight rate targeted by the Fed. | M01 §2.6.1 | 讲 p.28 |
| 市值加权 | Capitalization-weighted / value-weighted | Bigger companies take higher weight in the index. | M01 §2.8.2 | 🎙️`01:31:29` |

## 3. 组合与交易

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 组合权重 | Portfolio weight | The fraction of capital allocated to each asset; negative for short positions. | M01 §2.10.2 | 讲 p.15 |
| **多空组合** | Long-short position | A position that buys one asset and sells another. | M01 §2.10.2 | 讲 p.15 |
| **美元中性** | Dollar-neutral | Equal dollar weights long and short, so net dollar exposure is zero — **but not all risk is neutralized**. | M01 §2.10.2 | 讲 p.15 |
| 相对价值 / 配对交易 | Relative-value trade / Pairs trade | A position whose payoff depends on the relative performance of two related assets. | M01 §2.10.1 | 讲 p.8 |
| 再平衡 | Rebalance | Resetting portfolio weights to their targets each period. | M01 §2.10.2 | 讲 p.15 |
| **主动收益** | Active return | Stock return minus market return. | M01 §2.7.1 | 讲 p.41 |
| 交易成本 | Transaction cost | The cost of executing a trade, ignored in this course's exercises. | M01 §2.3 | 🎙️`02:03:48` |
| **买卖价差** | Bid-ask spread | A simple proxy for transaction cost. | M01 §2.3 | 🎙️`02:04:56` |
| 流动性 | Liquidity | How easily a position can be traded without moving the price. | M01 §2.3 | 🎙️`02:05:08` |
| 市场冲击 | Market impact | The price movement caused by one's own order. | M01 §2.3 | 🎙️`02:03:42` |
| 回测 | Backtest | Evaluating a strategy on historical data. | M01 §2.5.2 | 🎙️`29:19` |
| 夏普比率 | Sharpe ratio | 风险调整后收益（**M05 正式定义**） | M05（预告） | 🎙️`01:35:06` |

## 4. 数据时点纪律 ★ 本课核心

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **预测时钟** | Forecast clock | When the signal is formed and which future return is the target. | M01 §2.5.1 | 讲 p.10, 43 |
| **数据泄漏** | Data leakage | Using information in a predictor that was not observable at the time the forecast was made. | M01 §2.5.2 | 讲 p.48 |
| **前视偏差** | Look-ahead bias | Evaluating a historical strategy with information that only became available later; in M03 the professor uses the same term for published factors that were found by "looking back" at what already worked. | M01 §2.5.2 | 🎙️`01:41:52`；🎙️ M03 §2.6.6 `01:54:11`–`01:55:31`（"published…factors that discover[ed]…expose[d]…this is called look-ahead bias"） |
| **生存者偏差** | Survivorship bias | Keeping only assets that survived to today, which systematically overstates historical performance. | M01 §2.8.3 | 🎙️`01:41:52` |
| **冻结样本池** | Frozen universe / frozen panel | Fixing index membership as of a historical date so later membership changes cannot enter the sample. | M01 §2.8 | 讲 p.24, 25 |
| 历史成分股 | Historical constituents | The index membership as it actually stood at each past date. | M01 §2.8.3 | 讲 p.13 脚注 |
| **时点数据** | Point-in-time data | Data recorded as it stood on each date, rather than the currently revised series. | M01 §2.5.4 | 讲 p.13 脚注 |
| **参考期 / 观测月** | Reference period / observation month | The period a statistic describes — not the day investors could see it. | M01 §2.5.4 | 讲 p.27, 33 |
| **发布日** | Release date | The day a statistic became public. | M01 §2.5.4 | 讲 p.27 |
| **归档日** | Filing date | The day a 10-Q or 10-K was filed with the regulator. | M01 §2.6.3 | 讲 p.39 |
| 财季期末 | Fiscal period end | The last day of the accounting period a statement describes. | M01 §2.6.3 | 讲 p.39 |
| **数据修订 / 实时版本** | Revision / Vintage | Published values can be revised; without an archived vintage, today's history cannot establish exactly what was available at an earlier decision time. | M01 §2.6.1 | 讲 p.33 |
| **实时数据版本** | Vintage (ALFRED) | The version of a series as it stood at a past date, before later revisions. | M01 §2.6.1 | 讲 p.33 |
| **发布滞后** | Release lag | Extra waiting time added for safety: **+1 month for macro, +3 months for company financials**. | M01 §2.6.1 | 🎙️`01:41:24` |
| 三行手检 | Three-row check | A traceable spot check of predictor dates and target periods across three consecutive forecasts; it is not the only proof needed for a leakage-free dataset. | M01 §2.7.4 | 讲 p.47 |
| 静默插值 | Silent interpolation | Filling published gaps without saying so — explicitly forbidden. | M01 §2.6.1 | 讲 p.30, 32 |

## 5. 预测变量与建模

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **预测变量** | Predictor / feature | A variable used on the right-hand side to forecast a future return. | M01 §2.7 | 讲 p.10 |
| **特征表** | Feature table | One row per forecast period (and asset), with predictors available no later than the declared forecast cutoff and later realised return as target; equality at cutoff is allowed only when the data is actually released and accessible then. | M01 §2.7.1 | 讲 p.41, 46 |
| 目标 | Target | The realized return the row is trying to forecast. | M01 §2.7.2 | 讲 p.44 |
| **横截面** | Cross-section | The set of assets observed at one point in time. | M01 §2.8.1 | 讲 p.24 |
| 面板数据 | Panel data | Multiple assets observed over multiple periods. | M01 §2.8 | 💡 |
| **动量** | Momentum | `P_{t−1}/P_{t−k−1} − 1`, the cumulative price change known before the forecast period. | M01 §2.7.2 | 讲 p.44 |
| **均线偏离** | Moving-average gap | `P_{t−1} / mean(P_{t−k..t−1}) − 1`, distance from the recent trend. | M01 §2.7.2 | 讲 p.44 |
| **技术指标** | Technical indicator | A predictor computed from price and volume alone; it avoids external publication lags only under the stated data availability; future prices, centred windows or later revisions can still leak. | M01 §2.7.5 | 🎙️`01:56:43` |
| 利润率 | Profit margin | net income / revenue | M01 §2.6.4 | 讲 p.38 |
| 账面杠杆 | Book leverage | 1 − equity / assets | M01 §2.6.4 | 讲 p.38 |
| 资产增长 | Asset growth | assets / lagged assets − 1 | M01 §2.6.4 | 讲 p.38 |
| 现金流/资产 | Cash flow to assets | operating cash flow / assets | M01 §2.6.4 | 讲 p.38 |
| **市场有效性** | Market efficiency | A hypothesis about how quickly available information enters prices and how difficult abnormal returns are to earn; a noisy plot alone does not prove it. | M01 §2.9.3 | 🎙️`01:02:05` |
| **随机游走 / 鞅** | Random walk / Martingale | The best predictor of tomorrow's price is today's price. | M01 §2.9.3 | 🎙️`01:01:24` |
| 反转 | Reversal | The slight negative autocorrelation found in realized returns. | M01 §2.9.3 | 🎙️`01:02:30` |
| 另类数据 | Alternative data | Non-public datasets bought by investors to obtain information beyond public sources. | M01 §2.7.5 | 🎙️`02:02:27` |
| 内幕信息 | Inside information | Non-public information about a company; using it is illegal. | M01 §2.3 | 🎙️`25:13` |

## 5b. 回归与样本外评价（M02）

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 条件均值 | Conditional mean | Does $E[r_t\mid x_{t-1}]$ change with the predictor? | M02 §2.1 | 讲 L2 p.3 |
| 消费者价格指数 | Consumer Price Index (CPI) | A measure of changes in the price level of a basket of consumer goods and services; its reference month and public release date are different facts. | M02 §2.2.1（M01 已登记宏观序列） | 🎙️ 新闻例前的笔记释义 |
| 拟合线 | Fitted line | OLS chooses α̂ and β̂ to minimize squared residuals. | M02 §2.4.1 | 讲 L2 p.18 |
| 残差 | Residual | `ε̂_t = r_t − r̂_t`; residuals are data, not waste. | M02 §2.4.6 | 讲 L2 p.25 |
| 标准误 | Standard error | How much an estimate would vary across repeated samples generated by the same process. | M02 §2.4.3 | 讲 L2 p.22 |
| 等频分箱 | Equal-count bins | Sort by the predictor, split into ten groups of similar size, and average x and r within each group. **A diagnostic, not a substitute for the raw data.** | M02 §2.3.3 | 讲 L2 p.13 |
| 相关系数与简单回归 R² | Correlation and simple-regression R² | With the same non-missing rows, an intercept, no penalty, and nonzero variance in both columns, simple OLS has $R^2=\operatorname{corr}(x,y)^2$. | M02 §2.3.4 | 课堂加分题 + 三行笔记教学例 |
| 多元回归 | Multiple regression | How returns vary with one predictor while holding the others fixed. | M02 §2.5.1 | 讲 L2 p.28 |
| **厨房水槽（回归）** | Kitchen sink | Putting every available predictor into one regression; Welch and Goyal (2008 RFS) use it to show that stronger in-sample fit need not survive out of sample. | M02 §2.5.1 | 讲 L2 p.28 |
| 多重共线性 | Correlated predictors / multicollinearity | High predictor correlation can make individual slopes and t-tests unstable; a prediction combination may still be usable, but this must be checked out of sample. | M02 §2.5.2 | 讲 L2 p.30 |
| **训练集标准化** | Standardize using training data only | `z = (x − x̄_train)/s_train`; recomputing on the full sample **leaks future distribution information**. | M02 §2.5.3 | 讲 L2 p.31 |
| 按时间切分 | Chronological split | Earlier dates for fitting, later dates for evaluation; **never shuffle rows**. | M02 §2.6.2 | 讲 L2 p.7, 37 |
| 训练 / 验证 / 测试 | Training / Validation / Test | Estimate / choose / evaluate once. **Changing a model after inspecting the test result turns that period into development data.** | M02 §2.6.3 | 讲 L2 p.38 |
| 固定 / 扩展 / 滚动窗口 | Fixed holdout / Expanding / Rolling window | Every valid design preserves time order and fits before evaluating. | M02 §2.6.3 | 讲 L2 p.40 |
| 冻结规格 | Frozen design | Predictor names, training means and standard deviations, fitted coefficients, and test dates and row order all stay fixed. | M02 §2.6.4 | 讲 L2 p.45 |
| 均方误差 | MSE | `(1/T)·Σ(r_t − r̂_t)²` | M02 §2.7.2 | 讲 L2 p.43 |
| **样本外 R²** | Out-of-sample R² | `1 − Σ(r_t−r̂_t)²/Σ(r_t−r̂ᵇ_t)²`; positive means beating the stated benchmark. **Has no target-free meaning.** | M02 §2.7.2 | 讲 L2 p.43, 44 |
| 命中率 | Hit rate | `(1/T)·Σ 𝟙{sign(r̂_t)=sign(r_t)}` | M02 §2.7.2 | 讲 L2 p.43 |
| **正收益占比 / always-up 分数** | Positive-return base rate / always-up score | The share of positive-return months equals the score of always predicting up. It is not automatically the post-hoc majority-sign score or the only prespecified deployable benchmark. | M02 §2.7.3 | 讲 L2 p.47 |
| **滞后 MA(12) 基准** | Lagged MA(12) benchmark | `r̂ᵇ_{m,t} = (1/12)·Σ_{j=1..12} r_{m,t−j}`；数据集 `csi300_macro_panel.benchmark_ma12` 就是它 | M02 §2.7.3 | 讲 L2 p.44, 46 |
| 零主动收益基准 | Zero active-return benchmark | $\hat a^b_{i,t}=0$: stock i is expected to match its local market because active return is stock return minus local-market return. | M02 §2.7.3 | 讲 L2 p.44 |
| 零超额收益基准 | Zero excess-return benchmark | $\hat e^b_{i,t}=0$: stock i is expected to earn the matched risk-free return because the later data target subtracts the period-matched risk-free return. | M02 §2.7.3 口径衔接 | 后续数据包；不是 p.44 目标，仅登记差异，不升级 M03–M05 验收状态 |
| 有效市场假说 | Efficient Market Hypothesis (EMH) | Prices reflect a specified information set; weak, semi-strong, and strong forms use different sets. The classroom “within seconds” remark is a public-information example, not a claim that every monthly move is efficient. | M02 §2.1 | 🎙️ P1 `07:22` + 笔记限定 |
| F 检验（联合显著性） | F-test | Tests whether all slopes are zero at once. A significant F with insignificant individual t-tests is consistent with multicollinearity, but does not diagnose it by itself. | M02 §2.5.0 | 🎙️ 课堂 + 笔记限定 |
| 数据挖掘（贬义） | Data mining (p-hacking) | Trying many predictors until one clears p < 0.05; under 100 true nulls and valid 5% tests, the expected number of false positives is 5, not guaranteed to be exactly or at least 5（🎙️ P2 `32:42`）。⚠️ 与 IS6400 里褒义的 data mining 是同一个词 | M02 §2.6.1 | 🎙️ 课堂 + 笔记限定 |
| 发表后偏差 | Post-publication bias | Trading after publication may weaken a signal; later failure alone cannot distinguish this from overfitting or structural change. | M02 §2.6.1 | 🎙️ 课堂 + 笔记限定 |
| 历史均值基准 | Historical average | The forecast with all slopes set to zero — Campbell & Thompson (2008): hard to beat out of sample | M02 §2.6.1 | 讲 L2 p.36 + 🎙️ |
| 猴子基准 | "Monkey" benchmark | Always guessing “up”; its realized score equals the positive-return share. It is not automatically the post-hoc majority-sign score or a unique deployable rule. | M02 §2.1、§2.7.4 | 🎙️ 课堂 + 笔记限定 |
| 六条评价标准 | Six evaluation criteria | Sample association / forecast error / relative accuracy / direction / stability / economic value. | M02 §2.7.1 | 讲 L2 p.42 |

## 5c. 线性机器学习：收缩、降维与排序（M03）

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 超额收益 | Excess return | $r^e_{i,t} = r_{i,t} - r_{f,t}$, the return above a period-matched risk-free return. | M03 §2.6.5 | 讲 L3 p.33 🎙️ |
| 无风险收益代理 | Risk-free proxy | U.S. three-month Treasury yield (U.S., HKSAR); ChinaBond three-month yield (Chinese mainland); previous month-end value converted to the holding period. | M03 §2.6.5 | 讲 L3 p.33 |
| 收缩 | Shrinkage | Add a penalty for the overall size of slopes; correlated predictors can redistribute contributions, so an individual slope need not fall. | M03 §2.4.1 | 讲义+笔记限定 |
| 惩罚项 | Penalty | $\lambda P(\beta)$ added to the training loss; the intercept is left unpenalized. | M03 §2.4.1 | 讲 L3 p.12 |
| 超参数 | Hyperparameter | A setting (λ, ρ, K) chosen on validation data rather than estimated in the fit. | M03 §2.4.1 | 💡 |
| 前向选择 | Forward selection | Start with no predictors; add the predictor with the lowest validation MSE; stop when validation MSE no longer falls. | M03 §2.3 | 讲 L3 p.10 |
| 岭回归 | Ridge regression | A squared-slope penalty without an L1 threshold interval; an individual coefficient may still be exactly zero in special cases. | M03 §2.4.2 | 讲L3 p.13+笔记反例 |
| LASSO | Least Absolute Shrinkage and Selection Operator | Absolute-value penalty with a corner at zero: some fitted slopes become exactly zero. | M03 §2.4.3 | 讲 L3 p.15 |
| 软阈值 | Soft-thresholding | $\hat\beta = \operatorname{sign}(\hat\beta_{OLS})\max(\lvert\hat\beta_{OLS}\rvert - \lambda, 0)$ for one standardized input. | M03 §2.4.3 | 💡 |
| 弹性网 | Elastic Net | Mix L1 and L2 penalties in one objective; related signals may be retained together, but joint inclusion is not guaranteed. | M03 §2.4.4 | 讲L3 p.17+笔记限定 |
| 软件惩罚参数 | Software alpha | In scikit-learn, alpha denotes penalty strength; with $L = \text{SSE}/(2n)$, Ridge's software alpha = $n\lambda$; scales differ across implementations. | M03 §2.4.2 | 讲 L3 p.14, p.25 |
| 系数路径 | Coefficient path | Fitted slopes as a function of the penalty. | M03 §2.4.5 | 讲 L3 p.19 |
| 验证曲线 | Validation curve | Validation MSE as a function of the penalty; the minimum is the selected penalty. | M03 §2.4.5 | 讲 L3 p.20 |
| 股-周面板 | Stock-week panel | One row = one stock in one forecast week. | M03 §2.6.1 | 讲 L3 p.29 |
| 固定股票池 | Fixed universe | Membership is fixed at the start of the exercise; missing returns remain missing; later additions do not replace original members. | M03 §2.6.2 | 讲 L3 p.30 |
| 技术指标六族 | Six indicator families | Trend / bar geometry / activity / volatility / oscillator / market risk. | M03 §2.6.3 | 讲 L3 p.31 |
| 截面排名 | Cross-sectional rank | Rank of a characteristic inside the Hang Seng Index cross-section at one date. | M03 §2.6.4 | 讲 L3 p.32 |
| 中心化排名 | Centered rank | Average within-date rank divided by the valid stock count, minus 0.50; a finite-sample mean or median observation need not equal zero. | M03 §2.6.4 | 讲L3 p.32、课堂减0.5+笔记例 |
| 特征分组组合 | Characteristic-sorted portfolio | Five equal-weighted portfolios formed each week from one lagged characteristic. | M03 §2.6.6 | 讲 L3 p.36 |
| 降维 | Dimension reduction | Summarize many correlated inputs by a few components before regression. | M03 §2.7.1 | 讲 L3 p.40 |
| 主成分回归 | Principal Component Regression (PCR) | Choose directions using variation in training predictors alone, then fit the return regression on their component scores and observed returns. | M03 §2.7.2 | 讲L3 p.41+笔记步骤限定 |
| 主成分载荷 | Loading | Weight of each original characteristic in a component. | M03 §2.7.2 | 讲 L3 p.43 |
| 偏最小二乘 | Partial Least Squares (PLS) | Components chosen to maximize squared covariance with training excess returns; uses both Z and $r^e$. | M03 §2.7.3 | 讲 L3 p.44 |
| 常数预测 | Constant forecast | Identical forecasts provide no model ranking; their MSE can be better or worse than a zero benchmark. | M03 §2.8.4 | 讲L3 p.51+笔记反例 |
| 预测分组排序 | Forecast sort | Rank by predicted excess return before the holding week; assign five groups; compare realized returns. | M03 §2.9.1 | 讲 L3 p.53 |
| 高减低价差 | High-minus-low spread | Top forecast group's realized excess return minus the bottom group's. | M03 §2.9.1 | 讲 L3 p.54–55 |
| 预测精度与排序的分离 | Accuracy versus ranking | MSE assesses forecast levels; a sort assesses ordering. | M03 §2.9.2 | 讲 L3 p.54 |
| 阈值 · 交互 | Threshold · Interaction | Slope effects that change with a level or with another predictor — Class 4. | M03 §2.9.4 | 讲 L3 p.56（转录缺结尾，未涉及） |
| 主动收益 | Active return | Individual stock return minus the market return (not minus the risk-free rate). | M03 §2.6.5 | 🎙️ 讲义没有，教授口头提及（`01:20:14`），姊妹概念，本讲不用 |
| 斯皮尔曼等级相关 | Spearman's rank correlation | Correlation between the ranks of matched forecasts and realized outcomes; it measures ordering, not investment return.（笔记自拟） | M03 §2.9.2 | 见M03当地来源；英文为笔记自拟 |
| 小市值减大市值因子 | Small Minus Big (SMB) | The mean return of the three small size/value portfolios minus that of the three big portfolios in the stated French construction.（外源定义的笔记自拟英文） | M03 §2.6.4 | 见M03当地来源；英文为笔记自拟 |
| 高账面市值比减低账面市值比因子 | High Minus Low (HML) | The mean return of the two value portfolios minus that of the two growth portfolios in the stated French construction.（外源定义的笔记自拟英文） | M03 §2.6.4 | 见M03当地来源；英文为笔记自拟 |
| 做空 | Short selling | Borrow shares, sell them, then buy back and return the same quantity; profits and losses depend on the repurchase price.（笔记自拟） | M03 §2.9.3 | 见M03当地来源；英文为笔记自拟 |
| 总敞口 / 净敞口 | Gross / net exposure | Gross adds the absolute long and short amounts; net subtracts short from long, each relative to stated equity.（笔记自拟） | M03 §2.9.3 | 见M03当地来源；英文为笔记自拟 |

## 5d. 非线性机器学习：树、集成与神经网络（M04）

> 来自 [[M04-非线性机器学习与收益预测]] v0.9 课前预习版（无转录，英文定义取讲义原句）。

| 中文 | English | 英文定义（可默写） | 首现 | 来源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 回归树 | Regression tree | A tree divides observations into groups called leaves; in leaf $R_\ell$ the forecast is the mean training return. Forecasts differ across observable regimes. | M04 §2.2.2 | 讲 L4 p.5、p.14 |
| 叶子 | Leaf | A terminal group of training observations defined by a sequence of splits; its mean return is the forecast for any observation routed to it. | M04 §2.2.2 | 讲 L4 p.5、p.14 |
| 分裂准则 | Split criterion | At each node choose predictor $j$ and threshold $s$ to minimize the sum of squared deviations from the two child means; repeat within each child subject to depth and leaf-size limits. | M04 §2.2.3 | 讲 L4 p.6 |
| 截面分裂 | Cross-sectional split | In the same month, separate firms by a characteristic such as size; different stock groups can have different return relations. | M04 §2.2.4 | 讲 L4 p.7 |
| 时序分裂 | Time-series split | For the same market, separate months by a state such as lagged inflation; different market states can have different return relations. | M04 §2.2.4 | 讲 L4 p.7 |
| 深度 | Depth | The maximum number of successive questions from root to leaf; chosen on chronological validation data — deeper trees fit development returns more closely but forecast validation months worse. | M04 §2.2.7 | 讲 L4 p.11–12 |
| 最小叶大小 | Minimum leaf size | The smallest number of training observations a leaf may contain; a high-return leaf based on a few months is a noisier estimate than a similar leaf observed repeatedly. | M04 §2.2.8 | 讲 L4 p.13 |
| 交互效应 | Interaction | The effect of one signal depends on another (the momentum effect changes sign with volatility); a regression with only additive terms cannot reproduce it, a tree can split on volatility then momentum. | M04 §2.2.9 | 讲 L4 p.15 |
| 只做多 · 超配 / 低配 | Long-only · Overweight / underweight | A manager who cannot short expresses a negative view by holding less than the benchmark weight; Class 5 turns forecasts into constrained weights. | M04 §2.2.10 | 讲 L4 p.16 |
| bagging | Bagging (bootstrap aggregating) | Fit B trees independently on bootstrap samples drawn from training data with replacement and average their forecasts; more trees reduce the uncorrelated part of prediction variance, shared errors remain. | M04 §2.3.1 | 讲 L4 p.18–19 |
| 自助样本 | Bootstrap sample | A resample of the training rows drawn with replacement, the same size as the original; resampling uses training data only. | M04 §2.3.1 | 讲 L4 p.18–19 |
| 随机森林 | Random forest | Bagging plus, at each node, a search for the best split among a fresh random subset of predictors (5 of 30 here); random predictor selection reduces correlation between trees, making averaging more effective. | M04 §2.3.2 | 讲 L4 p.20–21 |
| 随机预测变量子集 | Random predictor subset | The $\lfloor\sqrt{p}\rfloor$ predictors considered at each split of a random-forest tree. | M04 §2.3.2 | 讲 L4 p.20–21 |
| 梯度提升 | Gradient boosting | $F_0 = \bar y_{\text{train}}$, $e_{im} = y_i - F_{m-1}(x_i)$, $F_m = F_{m-1} + \nu h_m$: fit corrections sequentially with small trees on current residuals; a forest averages trees, boosting adds successive corrections. | M04 §2.3.3 | 讲 L4 p.22–23 |
| 残差修正 | Residual correction | Each boosting step fits a small tree to the residuals of the current forecast and adds a scaled version of it. | M04 §2.3.3 | 讲 L4 p.22–23 |
| 学习率 | Learning rate ν | The fraction of each correction tree's forecast added at every boosting step; chosen together with tree count and depth on validation data. | M04 §2.3.3 | 讲 L4 p.22–23 |
| 早停 | Early stopping | Track validation loss as trees (or epochs) are added and stop when it no longer falls — the same decision as choosing complexity on validation, made one step at a time. | M04 §2.3.4 | 讲 L4 p.24 |
| 神经网络 | Neural network | Hidden units apply a nonlinear activation to weighted inputs; training learns the connection weights and intercepts; parameters minimize squared error plus weight shrinkage. | M04 §2.4.1 | 讲 L4 p.30 |
| 隐藏单元 | Hidden unit | A weighted sum of standardized inputs passed through a nonlinear activation, e.g. $h = \max(0, m - v)$. | M04 §2.4.1 | 讲 L4 p.30 |
| ReLU | ReLU activation | $\max(0, \cdot)$: negative inputs become zero, positive inputs pass unchanged. | M04 §2.4.1 | 讲 L4 p.30 |
| 权重收缩 | Weight shrinkage | The penalty $\frac{\lambda}{2}\sum_{w\in\mathcal W} w^2$ on connection weights (biases unpenalized), the same form as ridge. | M04 §2.4.2 | 讲 L4 p.31 |
| 训练轮数 | Epoch | One pass through the training data; the number of epochs is chosen by early stopping on validation weeks. | M04 §2.4.4 | 讲 L4 p.33 |
| 独立日期数 | Number of independent dates | Stocks in the same week share news and market shocks, so 12,281 stock-week rows cover 156 weekly dates, not 12,281 independent episodes; the 156 weeks are not guaranteed IID and may be serially dependent; keep every stock from a date together when splitting. | M04 §2.4.5 | 讲 L4 p.34–35 |
| 置换重要性 | Permutation importance | The increase in test MSE when one predictor's values are shuffled; it records how much the selected model relies on that predictor — not a regression coefficient or a causal effect. | M04 §2.5.1 | 讲 L4 p.36 |
| 政策公告（2024-09-24） | Policy announcement (24 Sep 2024) | The CSI 300 excess return of +18.9% in September 2024 that no June-2021 model anticipated; models retain their earlier fits, OOS $R^2$ in the recent 36-month window ranges from −43% to −180%. | M04 §2.5.2 | 讲 L4 p.37 |
| 成交额趋势排名 | Dollar-volume-trend rank | The centered cross-sectional rank of the trading-activity trend; the validation-tuned stock tree splits it at about 0.150 (65th percentile), test OOS $R^2$ −0.1% against zero. | M04 §2.6.3 | 讲 L4 p.43–44 |
| 验证平局 | Validation near-tie | All three nonlinear families have validation MSE within 26.25–26.64 (×10⁴); report the numbers and treat small differences cautiously. | M04 §2.6.4 | 讲 L4 p.45–46 |
| 冻结模型 | Preselected evaluation model | The model chosen on validation and reported on the test; do not switch after the test even if another candidate has lower test MSE. | M04 §2.6.5 | 讲 L4 p.47 |
| 投资授权 | Investment mandate | The constraints a manager operates under (long-only, concentration, risk); a model can perform differently under accuracy, ranking and mandate objectives — choose the objective before the final test. | M04 §2.7.5 | 讲 L4 p.52–53 |
| 信息集（缺失变量） | Information set · Missing predictive variable | More flexibility cannot compensate for a missing predictive variable; thirty overlapping indicators and short-period thresholds explain the limited test gains. | M04 §2.7.6 | 讲 L4 p.54 |

## 6. 数据源与机构

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 定义 | 首现 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Yahoo Finance / `yfinance` | — | 免费全球行情与财务数据接口，本课主力数据源 | M01 §2.4 | 讲 p.10 |
| AKShare | — | 面向中国市场的开源数据接口 | M01 §2.6.2 | 讲 p.29 |
| FRED | Federal Reserve Economic Data | 圣路易斯联储宏观数据库 | M01 §2.6.1 | 讲 p.28 |
| ALFRED | Archival FRED | FRED 的实时版本（vintage）数据库 | M01 §2.6.1 | 讲 p.33 |
| `quantmod` / `TTR` | — | R 语言的金融数据与技术指标包 | M01 §2.4.2 | 讲 p.12 |
| 10-Q / 10-K | — | 美国上市公司的季报 / 年报 | M01 §2.6.3 | 讲 p.27, 34 |
| SEC | U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission | 美国证券交易委员会 | M01 §2.6.3 | 讲 p.34 ＋ 🎙️ |
| SFC | Securities and Futures Commission | 香港证券及期货事务监察委员会 | M01 §2.6.3 | 🎙️`01:38:40` |
| **上证综指** | SSE Composite Index | 上海证券交易所综合指数——**不可直接交易**，媒体常引用，是评估收益时的常见错误 | M01 §2.3.3 | 🎙️`01:10:59` |
| **沪深 300** | CSI 300 | 可通过 ETF 投资，是 A 股的标准基准 | M01 §2.3.3 | 🎙️`01:11:26` |
| 恒生指数 | Hang Seng Index | 香港市场的主要指数 | M01 §2.4 | 讲 p.17 |
| **恒生科技指数** | HSTECH（Hang Seng TECH Index） | 30 只港股科技龙头（腾讯、阿里、美团、京东、小米等），本课个股练习的样本池 | M01 §2.8.1 | 讲 p.24 ＋ 🎙️`01:25:53` |
| 标普 500 | S&P 500 | 美国大盘基准 | M01 §2.4 | 讲 p.17 |
| SPY | SPDR S&P 500 ETF Trust | 跟踪 S&P 500 的 ETF；本课特征表的市场收益代理 | M01 §2.7.1 | 讲 p.41 |
| Bloomberg / Wind | — | 付费金融数据终端；CityU 有终端但需去机房，本课不需要 | M01 §2.6.4 | 🎙️`01:54:28` |

## 7. 课程与考核（大纲术语）

| 中文（统一译名） | English | 说明 | 源 |
|---|---|---|---|
| 持续评估 | Continuous assessment | 占 **60%** | 大纲 |
| 期末考试 | Final examination | 占 **40%**，**2 小时**，闭卷手写 | 大纲 ＋ 🎙️ |
| FinTech 公司案例报告 | FinTech company case report | 10%，≤10 页 | 大纲 |
| 录像展示 | Recorded video presentation | 20%，≤10 分钟，≤80 MB MP4 | 大纲 |
| ML 投资作业 | Machine-learning investment assignment | 20%，含报告 + 权重 CSV + 可复现代码包 | 大纲 |
| 参与与课堂表现 | Participation and in-class work | 10%，起始 5/10，答对 +1、缺席被点名 −1 | 大纲 ＋ 🎙️ |
| 点名提问 | Cold call | 教授按名单点名，不等志愿者 | 大纲 |
| 课程预期学习成果 | CILO / ILO | 官方目录 4 条 vs syllabus 4 条，**内容不同**，见 [[EF5560_Fintech_and_AI_in_Finance/_prep/课程前置资料\|课程前置资料]] §3.3 | 大纲 |
| 可复现性 | Reproducibility | 「Empirical work must preserve the data timing and transformation steps needed to reproduce the reported result.」 | 大纲 |
| 生成式 AI 政策 | Generative AI policy | 作业可用但须披露、最终版必须是自己的作品、**不得复制粘贴 AI 答案**；考试禁用 | 官方目录 |

